# hui AIR 214+K "PLASMA TRAP" — the mine's TIMER detonation (14z-78,
# maintainer-reported crash-reset). Phobos throws a mine in a downward arc;
# it lands, rolls forward slowly for roughly half a second (~1/6 screen),
# STOPS, and detonates into a small low-hitting dome of electricity. The
# crash is at that detonation, on every Phobos build ever made — the move
# appears in no other rig, gate or doc in this repo, which is why every gate
# was green while it crashed.
#
# WHAT THIS RIG HAS TO GET RIGHT (the 83d lesson, applied):
#   1. AIR. The move is air-only — 214+K on the ground is a different move.
#      P1 jumps and inputs the motion while RISING, so the mine is thrown
#      with height to arc down from.
#   2. THE TRIGGER IS A TIMER, NOT A COLLISION (maintainer-confirmed). So the
#      mine must be given room to land and roll UNDISTURBED: if it reaches
#      P2 the event captured is a contact explosion, which is a different
#      code path — exactly the error 83c made with the grenade. Both fighters
#      walk to their own corners first.
#   3. TIME. Land + roll (~30f) + detonate. Each attempt gets ~450 frames of
#      quiet afterwards; a rig that ends before the timer expires proves
#      nothing at all.
#   4. THREE STRENGTHS. Button strength sets the throw arc (83d), and the
#      maintainer said "214+K" without distinguishing. LK/MK/HK are fired in
#      turn so no single arc can be the reason nothing happened, and so a
#      strength-specific defect is still caught.
#
# VERDICT NOTE — a watchdog reset is NOT a 68k exception, so the crash guard
# can come back clean while the machine has rebooted. Watch P1 +0x382
# ($FF8782): 0x10 while he is alive, 0x00 once the watchdog has cleared RAM.
# That single bit also discriminates the two leading mechanisms: a FAULT
# means an out-of-range dispatch (the Cosmo shape), a silent REBOOT means an
# allocator spinning on an unseeded pool (Huitzil's own documented precedent).
#
# ── STATUS 14z-78: THIS RIG DOES NOT YET REPRODUCE THE CRASH ────────────
# Measured on build/hui27 (huitzil-m2), field_trace on
# ff8782/ff8406/ff8407, 6 attempts: LK/MK/HK x neutral and forward jump x
# motion at +14/+24/+34 frames after the jump.
#
#   * the rig is ARMED: p1char = 0x10 for all 3200 traced frames, so the
#     match forms with Phobos and the probe is live.
#   * actions DO fire on the button: seq 0x0E on the four early-motion
#     attempts; seq 0x02 -> 0x0A and 0x02 -> 0x08 on the two +34f ones,
#     which had probably already landed (ground moves, not the air special).
#   * NO crash and NO watchdog reset: p1char never leaves 0x10, the guard
#     reports 0 faults, and the replay runs to the end.
#
# So this is a fact about the RIG, not about the build — the maintainer
# reproduces the crash by hand on every Phobos build. seq 0x0E firing at
# exactly the button frame for every strength looks more like a plain
# jumping kick than Plasma Trap; the 214 motion is probably not registering
# in the air. Awaiting the maintainer on: which kick strength, what jump
# height/type, whether the motion is 214 relative to FACING, whether it
# needs meter, and roughly how many frames from throw to detonation.
#
# DO NOT promote this to a gate until it reproduces; a green here today
# would mean nothing.
#
# BOTH SIDES POKED: P1 = Huitzil (0x10), P2 = Victor (0x03 on vsav AND vsav2).
# Early window only (replay-80 rule).
# POKES="1400:ff8782:10;1450:ff8782:10;1500:ff8782:10;1400:ff8b82:03;1450:ff8b82:03;1500:ff8b82:03"
